  "sourcePolicy": {
    "classIdentity": "Pinned Chromium names this class Http2PriorityDependencies (formerly SpdyPriorityDependencies). Sources are net/spdy/http2_priority_dependencies.cc and .h.",
    "priorityConversion": "request_priority.h:28-45 defines HIGHEST=5, MEDIUM=4, IDLE=1. spdy_http_utils.cc:286-292 maps RequestPriority to SpdyPriority as 5 - priority; quic_http_utils.cc:14-20 uses the same 5 - priority for extensible urgency. Native u=4 corresponds to IDLE and renderer u=1 to MEDIUM in these scoped captured contexts.",
    "weightConversion": "Google spdy_protocol.cc:60-64 clamps SPDY priority to 0..7, computes float kSteps=255.9f/7.f, and returns static_cast<int>(kSteps*(7.f-priority))+1. The complete original routine and clamp execute unchanged for bands 0..7. Thus priority 4 maps to 110 and priority 1 to 220, matching all selected captured headers.",
    "registration": "SpdyStream::ProduceHeadersFrame spdy_stream.cc:129-143 calls SpdySession::CreateHeaders with its current priority. CreateHeaders spdy_session.cc:1076-1124 sets has_priority=true unconditionally, calls dependency OnStreamCreation before logging, then sets weight/parent/exclusive on SpdyHeadersIR and serializes it.",
    "creation": "Http2PriorityDependencies::OnStreamCreation lines22-51 ignores an already registered ID. Otherwise root parent 0 and exclusive=true are defaults, weight is converted from SPDY priority. PriorityLowerBound lines53-64 scans from the requested numeric band downward to 0, choosing the most recently appended stream in the first nonempty band. Append the new stream to its band. This is same-band latest live stream, else nearest higher-precedence nonempty band; not universally the previous stream ID.",
    "destruction": "OnStreamDestruction lines175-183 removes only that stream from its band and ID map. SpdySession::CloseActiveStreamIterator lines1847-1856 invokes it when the active stream is removed. SpdyStream lines459-467 and515-541 retain half-closed streams and close when both directions finish; reset/cancellation follows active-stream close paths. Do not remove dependency state merely when response headers arrive or only one direction finishes.",
    "priorityChange": "SpdySession::UpdateStreamPriority lines1230-1255 always updates queued-write priority, skips dependency updates while stream ID is 0, and skips wire reprioritization when kAvoidH2Reprioritization is enabled. Public features.cc:37 defaults that feature disabled. Otherwise OnStreamUpdate is called and returned updates are sent in order; EnqueuePriorityFrame lines1928-1950 puts all such frames at HIGHEST to serialize them.",
    "dependencyUpdate": "OnStreamUpdate lines111-173 returns empty for absent ID or unchanged priority. Find old parent, new lower-bound parent, and substitute old parent when the new lookup returns the moving stream itself. If parent changes, first reattach its old child to old parent/root with that child's mapped weight and exclusive=true, then reattach the moving stream to new parent/root with new mapped weight and exclusive=true. Finally remove the stream from the old band and append to the new band, even if no wire updates were required.",
    "serverNoRfc7540Setting": "Google spdy_protocol.h:163 defines SETTINGS_DEPRECATE_HTTP2_PRIORITIES as ID 0x9 (the no-RFC7540-priorities setting). SpdySession::HandleSetting lines2389-2408 accepts only 0/1; a changed value after the first SETTINGS drains with ERR_HTTP2_PROTOCOL_ERROR. Before the first SETTINGS completes, value 1 sets deprecate_http2_priorities_=true, while value 0 does not change it; its initial value is false. ALPS settings also pass through HandleSetting (spdy_session.cc:952-960). OnSettingsEnd:3112-3114 marks the first SETTINGS received.",
    "documentedHelperConditions": "SpdySession::ShouldSendHttp2Priority lines1045-1047 returns !enable_priority_update_ || !deprecate_http2_priorities_. ShouldSendPriorityUpdate lines1049-1055 is false when enable_priority_update_ is false; otherwise true before initial server SETTINGS, then equal to deprecate_http2_priorities_. The header comments document those conditions.",
    "helperUseLimit": "Neither CreateHeaders nor UpdateStreamPriority in the retained pinned source calls those helper functions. Initial HEADERS priority metadata is unconditional in CreateHeaders. Parsing server setting 9 and helper documentation alone do not prove actual suppression of that outgoing metadata in this pinned build; no such suppression is inferred here.",
    "logger": "NetLogSpdyHeadersSentParams spdy_session.cc:189-213 logs has_priority and, only when true, parent_stream_id/weight/exclusive supplied to the outgoing frame serializer. Capture fields therefore describe encoder inputs, not guessed stream policy."
  },
  "limits": [
    "Only selected native global/regional spclient and renderer Pathfinder HEADERS are covered. Other hosts and arbitrary renderer requests are outside this profile; the forced-H2 diagnostic is counted separately.",
    "Parent IDs are observed protocol stream IDs with source anchors. Full historical active-stream lifecycles and priority changes were not replayed from these captures, so parent-relation counts do not independently validate the complete dependency algorithm.",
    "Header priority presence, weight, exclusivity and dynamic parent inputs are directly captured. Selected unchanged public creation/destruction/weight routines execute on explicit synthetic inputs; no proprietary routine or original app executes.",
    "Live feature overrides, application scheduling, server behavior, HPACK/TLS bytes and complete frame/packet order remain unproved. No tests, production edits, app/account requests or probes are included."
  ]
}
